---
import Sub from '../layouts/Sub.astro';
import { cityPageSchema, SERVICE_PAGES } from '../data/site.js';

const description =
  'Concrete sealing in Washington, Utah — driveways, patios, pool decks and expansion joints across Coral Canyon, Green Springs and the rest of Washington City. Based next door in St. George.';

const schema = cityPageSchema({
  path: '/concrete-sealing-washington-ut',
  city: 'Washington',
  description,
});
---

<Sub
  title="Concrete Sealing in Washington, UT | Armour Crete"
  description={description}
  crumb="Washington, UT"
  schema={schema}
>
  <Fragment slot="h1">Concrete sealing<br />in Washington City.</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Washington is growing faster than almost anywhere in the county, and every
    one of those new driveways, patios and pool decks is starting the same clock
    against the same desert. We are based next door in St. George — close enough
    that the free assessment is genuinely free.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>24h</dt><dd>Cure before you walk or drive on it</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Deco</dt><dd>The only products we put down</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Free</dt><dd>On-site assessment, anywhere in Washington</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">Services in Washington, UT</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">Everything we do,<br />done here.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="chips rv">
        {SERVICE_PAGES.map((s) => <li><a href={s.href}>{s.label}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
      <div class="prose rv" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <p>
          From Coral Canyon to Green Springs to the older streets near the fields,
          the work is the same four steps: clean, dry, seal, cure — with prep
          first when the surface needs it, and a
          <a class="tlink" href="/products">named Deco product</a> matched to the
          exposure rather than whatever was on the truck.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-dark">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="rv">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-lt">Why here, why now</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">New concrete is the<br />best time to seal.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose rv">
        <p>
          A lot of Washington's concrete is young, and young concrete has a
          window: once it has fully cured and given up its moisture, sealing it
          protects a surface that has not yet taken damage — which beats
          restoring one that has. The desert does not wait long. Hundred-degree
          summer slabs, winter nights below freezing, salt pools and softener
          discharge all start working on an unsealed surface from year one.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your build is recent, the assessment tells you whether the slab is
          ready yet. If your street is one of the older ones, it tells you what
          prep comes first. Either way it costs nothing and commits you to
          nothing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">Washington questions</p>
        <h2 class="display sec-h">Asked in<br />Washington.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq rv">
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>Do you charge to come out to Washington?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            No. The on-site assessment is free everywhere we work, and Washington
            is a few minutes from our base in St. George.
          </p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>Our subdivision is brand new. When can our driveway be sealed?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            Once the concrete has fully cured and given up its moisture — sealing
            too early is how finishes fail. Tell us the pour date and we will
            schedule it properly.
          </p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="qa">
          <summary>Do you work with HOAs here?</summary>
          <div class="qa-b"><p>
            Yes — common-area flatwork, joint work and sealing, bid from a site
            visit with a scope document that says exactly what goes down and
            where.
          </p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Sub>
